---
import PhoneMock from "./PhoneMock.astro";
import Wave from "./Wave.astro";

// Minimal stroke icons (24x24 viewBox paths).
const facts = [
  {
    icon: "M4 5h16v11H8l-4 4V5z",
    title: "WhatsApp and Telegram",
    body: "No app to install. Learners use the messaging app already on their phone.",
  },
  {
    icon: "M12 3a9 9 0 100 18 9 9 0 000-18zM3 12h18M12 3c3 3 3 15 0 18M12 3c-3 3-3 15 0 18",
    title: "Language chosen in the bot",
    body: "Learners pick a language at registration and can change it any time.",
  },
  {
    icon: "M12 12a4 4 0 100-8 4 4 0 000 8zM4 21a8 8 0 0116 0",
    title: "A profile, not just a number",
    body: "A one-minute registration captures role, region and background, so the coach and the programme know who is learning.",
  },
  {
    icon: "M12 3a9 9 0 100 18 9 9 0 000-18zM12 7v5l3 3",
    title: "Available around the clock",
    body: "The coach answers at 6 am before market day and at 10 pm after the books are closed.",
  },
];
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="reveal py-20 lg:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 md:px-12 xl:px-6">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alp-green">How it works</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-alp-navy sm:text-4xl">
        One coach, four ways to learn
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-alp-muted">
        Learners follow structured courses or simply ask. Both draw on the same validated ALP content.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
      <!-- Learn -->
      <article class="flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-alp-border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-alp-navy/10">
        <div class="mb-6 h-[360px] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-alp-surface px-4 pt-6">
          <PhoneMock compact label="Lesson preview">
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 1">
              <p>Cash flow and budgets. Please choose from:</p>
              <p>1. Cash flow budget<br />2. Cash reserves<br />3. Learning path menu</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-user" style="--i: 2">1</div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 3">
              Does my business need a cash budget? Consider an agro retail shop that recently bought a new
              pickup for deliveries but now can't cover the rent due to poor cash management.
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach pm-voice" style="--i: 4" aria-label="Lesson audio, 12 seconds">
              <span class="pm-play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <Wave bars={16} />
              <span class="pm-time">0:12</span>
            </div>
          </PhoneMock>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alp-green">Learn</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug text-alp-navy">Short lessons you can read or listen to</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-alp-muted">
          Each ALP course is delivered as a sequence of short messages with an audio version of every lesson.
          Learners move at their own pace, and the coach remembers where they stopped.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Check -->
      <article class="flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-alp-border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-alp-navy/10">
        <div class="mb-6 h-[360px] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-alp-surface px-4 pt-6">
          <PhoneMock compact label="Quiz preview">
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 1">
              <p>Cash budgets are important, because:</p>
              <p>A) They provide valuable information for management decisions.<br />
              B) They help identify discrepancies between actual and expected performance.<br />
              C) Both of the above.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-user" style="--i: 2">B</div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 3">
              <p>Nice try! But not quite correct. The correct answer is C.</p>
              <p>Cash budgets are important for both reasons. They provide valuable information for
              management decisions and help owners identify discrepancies between actual and expected
              performance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 4">
              <p>Congratulations, you have completed 40% of the Cash flow and budgets category.</p>
              <p>1. Go to next course<br />2. Cash flow and budgets</p>
            </div>
          </PhoneMock>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alp-green">Check</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug text-alp-navy">A quiz after every lesson</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-alp-muted">
          Quick questions confirm understanding before moving on. Wrong answers get an explanation, right
          answers unlock the next course, and progress is shown as the learner goes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Ask -->
      <article class="flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-alp-border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-alp-navy/10">
        <div class="mb-6 h-[360px] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-alp-surface px-4 pt-6">
          <PhoneMock compact label="Question preview">
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-user" style="--i: 1">My customer says my price is too high. What should I do?</div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 2">
              <p>To address your customer's concern about your price being too high, you can consider the
              following strategies:</p>
              <p>1. Adjust your price: evaluate if you can slightly lower your price while still covering
              your costs and maintaining a profit.</p>
              <p>2. Emphasize value and benefits: highlight the quality, customer service or convenience
              that justify the current price.</p>
              <p>3. Offer promotions or discounts: limited-time offers attract customers without
              permanently lowering your prices.</p>
              <p class="pm-meta">Ask another question, or type 0 for the main menu</p>
            </div>
          </PhoneMock>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alp-green">Ask</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug text-alp-navy">A coach that answers from ALP content only</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-alp-muted">
          Type a question at any time. Answers are grounded in the validated ALP curriculum rather than
          general internet knowledge, and include diagrams and images where they help.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Speak -->
      <article class="flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-alp-border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-alp-navy/10">
        <div class="mb-6 h-[360px] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-alp-surface px-4 pt-6">
          <PhoneMock compact label="Voice preview">
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-user pm-voice" style="--i: 1" aria-label="Voice message, 4 seconds">
              <span class="pm-play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <Wave bars={14} />
              <span class="pm-time">0:04</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach" style="--i: 2">
              Record every item that comes in and goes out on the same day, in one book or sheet. Count
              your stock at the end of each week and compare it with the book, so you notice any difference
              early.
            </div>
            <div class="pm-bubble pm-coach pm-voice" style="--i: 3" aria-label="Spoken answer, 18 seconds">
              <span class="pm-play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <Wave bars={16} />
              <span class="pm-time">0:18</span>
            </div>
          </PhoneMock>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alp-green">Speak</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug text-alp-navy">Voice in, voice out</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-alp-muted">
          Learners who prefer speaking can send a voice note and hear the reply. Voice works in the
          learner's chosen language, so the coach sounds local rather than translated.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {
        facts.map((f) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-alp-surface p-6">
            <svg class="h-7 w-7 text-alp-green" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d={f.icon}></path>
            </svg>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-bold text-alp-navy">{f.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-alp-muted">{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
